{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":6,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1541469874,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDE1OlVzZXJDb250ZW50RWRpdDE0ODM3ODA1Mg=="},"target":"a529a36396a52fb6317eb3c67d0863899532bac9d79283d2e91f039fd2210a1e","message":"Would it be possible to turn datalad into \"a new unix shell\" in a way that people could execute their usual shell commands and/or scripts with the shebang #!/bin/datalad such that the shell would then interpret the commands, convert them to proper datalad syntax generating provenance but removing the overhead of learning datalad/git syntax?","files":null},{"type":2,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1541469891,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDE3OlJlbmFtZWRUaXRsZUV2ZW50MTk0Nzg0OTEwNA=="},"title":"#!datalad","was":"#!datalad"},{"type":5,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1541471632,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDE5NDc4ODE5NjQ="},"added":["enhancement"],"removed":[]},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1541472294,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQzNjExMjUyMg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2979#issuecomment-436112522"},"message":"Thanks @theovanerp for chiming in.\nNote that if you already have a script you could just `datalad run` it and thus record its effect within git history.  Indeed to gain the most of benefit from using `run` you would need to specify `--input` and `--output` arguments.\nBut if we \"marry\" datalad to reprozip (kudos to @remram44 and the team) with ability to trace/deduce input/outputs, and then even possibly if we hook into pre-call state of syscalls to call `datalad get` needed annexed files, then it could get quite cool. But even then I am not quite certain if it would warrant `datalad` in a shebang as opposed to just calling smth like `datalad run --with-trace script`, which would have benefit to work on any script, not just a shell script.\nI guess all of this also is very related to the https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2063, in particular to suggested there `--record-runs` option (i even forgot that I did suggest that ;-) -- thanks github Search).","files":null}]}